so i don't want your toe pointing straight forward i want you to touch get up touch and then angle that toe out about 45 degrees load and drive up to that next spot okay we're going all 15 feet turn around bring it back on the other side this drill is great for improving our change of direction ability and our overall quickness

03:13:29.508 --> 03:13:57.523
the line rotational agility we need a line that's 15 feet in length all we're going to do is we're going to jab i'm going to come back out on both feet and i'm going to go with a half spin so i'm going to rotate towards the wall right now half spin get my right foot on half spin come back to neutral i move up a little bit each time okay so very slow here it's left foot jab both feet out rotation right foot jab

03:13:57.503 --> 03:13:59.567
both feet out, and we're back in.

03:14:03.094 --> 03:14:09.347
Every single time, my foot is hitting that line because I need to really know where my feet are in space.

03:14:09.868 --> 03:14:12.693
Once we get that pattern, we got to start to really speed it up.

03:14:13.014 --> 03:14:15.799
So once I get down to the end, I'm going to switch over.

03:14:16.140 --> 03:14:18.685
So now my right foot is that initial jab.

03:14:18.968 --> 03:14:23.074
and my left foot is the jab after the half spin, okay?

03:14:23.094 --> 03:14:25.959
Jab, half spin, jab, half spin.

