04:56:18.637 --> 04:56:44.982
of the range of motion now one mistake that people make is they end up going into hyper extension i just want you in full extension so that your head and your heel are in one flat line i don't want your head to be back beyond your heels all right if you do not have the back extension machine you're going to do the alternative exercise which is the reverse plank so we're going to get the two benches we're going to hold in our normal reverse plank position that you've done before

04:56:44.962 --> 04:56:47.649
and now you should be strong enough to start loading up.

04:56:47.950 --> 04:56:50.858
So maybe put a 25 pound plate right on your hip.

04:56:51.179 --> 04:56:53.225
If that's too light, 45 pound plate.

04:56:53.566 --> 04:56:59.983
If that's too light, then just start stacking plates and hold them and have a friend take them on and off for each set.

04:56:59.963 --> 04:57:02.988
we are doing the back extension or the reverse plank.

04:57:03.008 --> 04:57:08.416
We are really targeting the glutes and we're really targeting them at that hip extension.

04:57:08.516 --> 04:57:11.861
So when we sprint, that is where that main torque is.

04:57:12.141 --> 04:57:15.166
That's where the big torque is through the hips near extension.

04:57:15.206 --> 04:57:17.910
So we can't just get that through squats and deadlifts.

04:57:18.190 --> 04:57:23.498
That's why exercises like the back extension or the reverse plank are so important.

04:57:23.799 --> 04:57:24.520
