05:47:42.641 --> 05:47:44.243
Let's just get as low as we can there.

05:47:44.724 --> 05:47:47.407
One, two, three, and back up.

05:47:47.467 --> 05:47:49.470
So three there, three there.

05:47:49.810 --> 05:47:54.055
I'm going to go five cycles, and then I'm going to switch to the other side.

05:47:54.576 --> 05:47:56.198
Five and five, same thing.

05:47:56.178 --> 05:47:59.603
For the adductor hip flexor combo, I'm going lateral with one skip.

05:47:59.663 --> 05:48:02.107
So it's one skip lateral, and I'm going down.

05:48:02.167 --> 05:48:03.349
I'm trying to touch this floor.

05:48:03.809 --> 05:48:08.797
Keep this knee straight because I want to get that stretch on the inside of the leg in this adductor.

05:48:09.117 --> 05:48:16.028
I'm going back with the hip like I would in a normal squat, and I'm getting nice and low, touch the floor, and I'm popping out to that other side.

05:48:16.528 --> 05:48:19.553
All right, so let's just hold about one second at the bottom.

05:48:19.533 --> 05:48:41.153
and pop out i need five of these down and back so it's 10 total and then i immediately go into a hip flexor same thing with the skip and now i land i turn this foot forward i pivot i'm here knee a couple inches off the floor i'm gonna rotate hold one and then come back and it's to the other side

05:48:46.128 --> 05:48:52.656
At the bottom of this stretch, I'm gonna get that really good stretch in the hip flexor, and I always need to turn towards the lead leg.

