Don't make the mistake of going here.

05:48:54.518 --> 05:49:02.568
You need to rotate towards that lead leg as far as we can, and I'm gonna feel it through that hip flexor, and then I pop out to the other side.

05:49:02.688 --> 05:49:08.555
For the overhead deep squat progression, I'm going high with the hands, basic squat stance, so I'm a little wider than shoulder width.

05:49:08.635 --> 05:49:12.540
I can point the toes out just a little bit, and then I'm just gonna go here,

05:49:12.520 --> 05:49:31.002
it's going to be a hamstring stretch one two three keep the hands down and come into a deep squat try to stay back on your heels if you can one two three rock forward so i'm on my toes now drive the knees out with the elbows hold one

05:49:30.982 --> 05:49:50.222
two, three, rock it back, heels back down to the ground, one, two, three, I need one hand up, two hand up, not out here, we need it back behind the head, and stand, alright, so that's one cycle, we're going to go for three of these, so it's one, two, three,

05:49:50.557 --> 05:49:52.820
One, two, three, lean.

05:49:53.601 --> 05:49:55.864
One, two, three, heels back down.

05:49:55.924 --> 05:49:59.949
One, two, three, one up, two up, stand, all right?

05:50:00.230 --> 05:50:08.561
If you cannot get down in that deep position, then let's just go as low as we can right here, and then on the lean, it's just gonna look like this, all right?

05:50:08.581 --> 05:50:12.946
And then we're gonna come back, hopefully parallel to the floor, one up, two up, stand.

05:50:13.307 --> 05:50:19.635
We just gotta get as low as we can, and every day try to progress so that we can get lower and lower, better range of motion.

05:50:19.615 --> 05:50:22.458
So for the hip bridge, it's gonna be a very basic hip bridge.

05:50:22.498 --> 05:50:24.820
Even if you're an advanced athlete, I want you to do this version.

05:50:25.221 --> 05:50:27.983
So we're gonna get up nice and flat in a hip bridge.

05:50:28.324 --> 05:50:30.025
I need to be flat through the hips.

05:50:30.326 --> 05:50:32.728
I'm driving through my midfoot right now.

05:50:33.248 --> 05:50:37.693
And now I'm just gonna squeeze my glutes together as hard as I possibly can.

05:50:38.053 --> 05:50:40.856
So just holding in this position isn't that difficult.

05:50:41.116 --> 05:50:48.964
But if I squeeze my glutes together as hard as I can so they're rock solid, I'm gonna get a really good isometric contraction.

05:50:48.944 --> 05:50:51.289
And I'm going to activate a lot of muscle fibers.

05:50:52.371 --> 05:50:59.325
And we're just going to hold in this position for 25 seconds with a full squeeze and then relax.

05:50:59.345 --> 05:51:03.474
This is all for hip activation, getting those glutes fired up.

05:51:03.494 --> 05:51:05.237
It's the most powerful muscle in the body.

05:51:05.478 --> 05:51:07.662
So we got to get them revved up for our session.

05:51:31.537 --> 05:51:35.546
So for my freestyle agility, I need you to get in your bag.

05:51:35.586 --> 05:51:37.290
I just need you to get loose, all right?

05:51:37.991 --> 05:51:42.962
So much of footwork is about rhythm, timing, and just creativity.

05:51:43.042 --> 05:51:47.632
So you can't always be put in this box where I'm telling you to move your feet like this.

05:51:48.053 --> 05:51:51.621
I need you to start to do it intuitively and be creative with it.

05:51:51.601 --> 05:51:54.484
All we're going to do is just freestyle with our footwork.

05:51:54.885 --> 05:51:56.747
For me, I like to pretend like I have a ball.

05:51:57.047 --> 05:52:02.314
We're not going to actually do it with a ball because we move a little faster and we cut a little harder without the ball.

05:52:02.334 --> 05:52:05.838
